# Pull requests only

Never work on `main`. Do not commit, push, or merge into `main` from a local checkout.

- Create a branch from the latest `origin/main`.
- Commit the change on that branch.
- Push the branch and open a pull request.
- Wait for the pull request. Do not merge it unless the user asks.

```text
# Bad
git checkout main
git commit
git push origin main

# Good
git checkout -b feat/short-name origin/main
git commit
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create
```
